        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Verbatim/comment tags without inner whitespace are no longer handled",
        "explanation": "This hunk removes the verbatim state machine from create_token. Raw-block handling now depends only on the lexer regexes, and those regexes require whitespace after the tag opener. `_raw_start_re` uses `{%\\s+(?:comment|verbatim)`, while `_verbatim_end_re` and `_comment_end_re` use `{%[^\\S\\n]+end...`. The old code stripped the tag content, so `{%verbatim%}`, `{%endverbatim%}` and `{%endcomment%}` all worked, and `tag_re` still accepts these forms. Under the new code: (a) A template whose only raw tag is `{%verbatim%}...{%endverbatim%}` takes the fast `tag_re.split` path. Its contents are lexed as normal VAR/BLOCK tokens, so `{{ x }}` renders as '' instead of the literal text, and unknown tags inside raise TemplateSyntaxError. (b) `{% verbatim %}...{%endverbatim%}` or `{% comment %}...{%endcomment%}` never finds its closing regex. The rest of the template becomes one TEXT token, and the result is an 'Unclosed tag' TemplateSyntaxError. (c) Whether `{%verbatim%}` is honoured now depends on whether some other `{% comment`/`{% verbatim` tag appears elsewhere in the template. Templates that used to work will now render differently or fail.",
        "suggestion": "Use `\\s*` (or `[^\\S\\n]*`) after BLOCK_TAG_START in `_raw_start_re`, `_comment_end_re` and `_verbatim_end_re`, to match the old `.strip()` behaviour. Add tests for `{%verbatim%}...{%endverbatim%}` and `{% comment %}...{%endcomment%}`.",
        "evidence": "return Token(token_type_match[token_start], content, position, lineno)",
        "confidence": 0.6,
        "id": "9b062af04e77",
